From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mindone <mindone@localhost>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] healthloop: do not re-arm the wake alarm that woke the loop

On battery the wake alarm runs at periodic_chores_interval_slow, and
MainLoop() re-arms it with timerfd_settime() whenever epoll_wait()
returns events, before the handlers run. timerfd_settime() resets the
expiration count, so when the alarm itself is one of those events the
non-blocking read() in WakeAlarmEvent() fails with EAGAIN, logs
"wakealarm_event: read wakealarm fd failed" and skips PeriodicChores():
every slow alarm wakeup is lost.

Re-arm only when the wake alarm is not among the returned events. A
fired alarm keeps its periodic interval, so the slow cadence is
unchanged.

---
diff --git a/health/utils/libhealthloop/HealthLoop.cpp b/health/utils/libhealthloop/HealthLoop.cpp
index 8501f33..78c762d 100644
--- a/health/utils/libhealthloop/HealthLoop.cpp
+++ b/health/utils/libhealthloop/HealthLoop.cpp
@@ -267,11 +267,19 @@ void HealthLoop::MainLoop(void) {
             break;
         }
 
+        bool wakealarm_fired = false;
+        for (int n = 0; n < nevents; ++n) {
+            auto* event_handler = reinterpret_cast<EventHandler*>(events[n].data.ptr);
+            if (event_handler != nullptr && event_handler->fd == wakealarm_fd_.get()) {
+                wakealarm_fired = true;
+            }
+        }
+
         /*
          * Reset slow timer to avoid excessive wakeup on interrupt
          * It's assumed periodic_chores_interval_slow means the device being in non-charging state
          */
-        if (nevents > 0 &&
+        if (nevents > 0 && !wakealarm_fired &&
             wakealarm_wake_interval_ == healthd_config_.periodic_chores_interval_slow) {
             WakeAlarmSetInterval(wakealarm_wake_interval_);
         }
